 {"id": "5953badcb184", "title": "Implement LSP semantic tokens (full-document) for apexls", "description": "## What\nAdd LSP `textDocument/semanticTokens/full` support to apexls-server, so editors get binder-grade semantic highlighting (fields vs. locals vs. static calls vs. unresolved) instead of TextMate-guess syntax coloring. This is the #1 priority gap in `.scratch/apex-lsp-gaps/research.md` (section 3, item 1).\n\n## Where\nAll code changes are in exactly two files:\n\n1. `crates/apexls-server/src/lib.rs` -- follow the pattern of `Backend::document_highlight` at line 1087 verbatim: snapshot `documents.version`, `wait_for_rebuild`, read `bind.program`, delegate to `capabilities::semantic_tokens_full(program, file, encoding)`. Add the `semantic_tokens_full` handler on the `LanguageServer` impl. Declare `semantic_tokens_provider` in `ServerCapabilities` in `Backend::initialize` (starting ~line 669). Emit the exact same `SemanticTokensLegend` your walker consumes -- keep it in one `const`/`fn` and reuse it in both the capability declaration and the walker so they can't drift.\n\n2. `crates/apexls-server/src/capabilities.rs` -- add `pub(crate) fn semantic_tokens_full(program: &BoundProgram, file: FileId, encoding: PositionEncoding) -> SemanticTokens` next to the other capability functions (see `document_highlights` at line 653 or `folding_ranges` at line 703 as reference shape). This function walks `apex-binder`'s `SymbolTable`/`Resolution` data for `file`, produces sorted-by-position tokens, and LSP-delta-encodes them (`deltaLine`, `deltaStart`, `length`, `tokenType`, `tokenModifiers`).\n\n## Token legend (start narrow, expand later)\nPick a minimal-but-useful subset of the LSP standard `SemanticTokenType`s that maps cleanly to what `apex-binder`'s `Resolution`/`SymbolKind` already distinguishes. Suggested v1:\n- Types: `class`, `interface`, `enum`, `type` (fallback), `typeParameter`\n- Callables: `method`, `function` (bare-call / trigger)\n- Values: `property` (Apex field / SObject field), `variable` (local), `parameter`, `enumMember`\n- Other: `namespace` (System, Schema, etc.), `keyword` only if you emit one for annotations (`@isTest`, `@AuraEnabled`)\n\nModifiers: `static`, `readonly` (for `final` locals + immutable stdlib fields), `declaration` (on the defining occurrence), `deprecated` (if binder tracks it -- else skip), `defaultLibrary` (for stdlib symbols).\n\nDo NOT invent custom token types -- clients only theme the standard set reliably.\n\n## Data source\n`apex-binder` already classifies every identifier occurrence: see `crates/apex-binder/src/symbol.rs` (`SymbolKind`, `ModifierSet`), `crates/apex-binder/src/resolve.rs` (per-reference resolutions), and how `capabilities::document_highlights` / `capabilities::references` already walk the binder for occurrences. You are producing the token list from resolved-reference data that already exists; no new binder pass is needed. If some fine-grained detail truly isn't available, drop that token rather than adding a binder pass -- v1 explicitly favors coverage-over-fidelity.\n\n## Encoding\nLSP semantic tokens are delta-encoded: emit tokens sorted by (line, start), then encode each as 5 u32s relative to the previous token. Respect the negotiated `PositionEncoding` via `line_index` -- same helper the other capability functions already use to convert offsets to LSP positions.\n\n## Explicitly OUT of scope for this task\n- `textDocument/semanticTokens/range` -- do NOT implement; v1 is full-document only. The `semantic_tokens_provider.range` field stays `Some(false)` (or absent).\n- `textDocument/semanticTokens/full/delta` -- do NOT implement; the `full.delta` field stays `Some(false)` (or absent). Return `SemanticTokens { result_id: None, data: [...] }`.\n- No changes to `apex-binder`, `apex-parser`, `apex-syntax`, `apex-metadata`, `apex-stdlib`. If you find yourself needing to add a field to the binder for a token you want to emit, drop the token -- v1 uses only data that already exists.\n\n## Acceptance\n- `cargo check -p apexls-server` passes.\n- `cargo clippy -p apexls-server --all-targets -- -D warnings` passes.\n- `ServerCapabilities` returned from `initialize` includes a populated `semantic_tokens_provider` with the same legend the walker uses.\n- The handler follows the `wait_for_rebuild` + `bind.program` pattern used by every other capability handler in `lib.rs`.\n- Inline unit tests in `capabilities.rs` (small `#[cfg(test)] mod tests`) cover: (a) delta-encoding of two tokens on the same line, (b) delta-encoding across lines, (c) a stdlib-static-member call emits `defaultLibrary` modifier, (d) a local variable reference emits `variable` (not `property`).\n\nA separate QA task (created after this) adds an integration test through the LSP transport; do NOT add that integration test in this task.", "role": "backend", "priority": 1, "scope": "medium", "complexity": "medium", "estimated_minutes": 720, "status": "open", "task_type": "standard", "upgrade_details": null, "depends_on": [], "parent_task_id": null, "depends_on_repo": null, "owned_files": ["crates/apexls-server/src/lib.rs", "crates/apexls-server/src/capabilities.rs"], "assigned_agent": null, "result_summary": null, "tenant_id": "default", "cell_id": null, "repo": null, "batch_eligible": false, "eu_ai_act_risk": "limited", "approval_required": false, "risk_level": "medium", "slack_context": null, "version": 1, "claimed_at": null, "completed_at": null, "closed_at": null, "claimed_by_session": null, "parent_session_id": null, "subtask_wait_started_at": null, "parent_context": null, "retry_count": 2, "max_retries": 3, "retry_delay_s": 0.0, "terminal_reason": null, "max_output_tokens": null, "meta_messages": ["Retry 1: Previous attempt failed with reason: Agent backend-2292e2df died; janitor failed: [\"file_contains: crates/apexls-server/src/lib.rs :: semantic_tokens_provider (unverified: absence claim for 'crates/apexls-server/src/lib.rs :: semantic_tokens_provider' has no coverage record)\", \"file_contains: crates/apexls-server/src/capabilities.rs :: semantic_tokens_full (unverified: absence claim for 'crates/apexls-server/src/capabilities.rs :: semantic_tokens_full' has no coverage record)\"]", "Retry 2: Previous attempt failed with reason: Agent backend-6b07651f died; janitor failed: [\"file_contains: crates/apexls-server/src/lib.rs :: semantic_tokens_provider (unverified: absence claim for 'crates/apexls-server/src/lib.rs :: semantic_tokens_provider' has no coverage record)\", \"file_contains: crates/apexls-server/src/capabilities.rs :: semantic_tokens_full (unverified: absence claim for 'crates/apexls-server/src/capabilities.rs :: semantic_tokens_full' has no coverage record)\"]"], "metadata": {"budget_multiplier": 1.0, "original_task_id": "816051c0dec2", "retry_of": "e8a5cdff48a2", "retry_mode": "cold", "retry_requested_mode": "warm", "retry_decision_hash": "165d210259988401efc1c6b2368e1dcdde1a9ec3447189e320bd9c1ddaaac780", "retry_downgrade_reason": "no_checkpoint"}, "max_turns": null}
